  "reason": "RNA-only multiprofile scvi_n200 is currently strong (≈0.65 accuracy/F1), but image evidence is sparse and weak: ResNet50 multiprofile avgpool reaches only 0.328 accuracy/0.288 F1. The key uncertainty is whether image performance is limited by the ResNet50 encoder or by a general lack of useful image signal. config_014 tests this by swapping in ImageNet ViT-L while keeping multiprofile and avgpool fixed, giving a clean comparison to config_011. This is the best next budget use because it isolates image representation, avoids jumping to multimodal fusion, and will clarify whether image modality is worth pursuing in later multimodal experiments."
